{
  "item": "Ghost01",
  "mu_name": "Ghost",
  "mu_name_from": "MuMain's _enum.h:4157: MONSTER_MODEL_GHOST = 7, and MODEL_GHOST_MONSTER = MODEL_MONSTER01 + 7 (:4932), so OpenMonsterModel loads Monster08.bmd; the server's type is MONSTER_GHOST = 11 (:4386). The client's name is 고스트, the English word in Hangul (ZzzCharacter.cpp:14102). OpenMU's Version075 Dungeon.cs:746-776 names number 11 'Ghost' at level 32 with 1000 health, 110-115 damage, 40 defense, MoveRange 3, AttackRange 1, ViewRange 5, AttackDelay 1400, respawn 10 s, no AttackSkill, resistances P2 I2 W2 F2. The Dungeon's commonest breed: 52 spots in Dungeon 1 and 5 in Dungeon 2 (docs/dungeon-port.md A §1.6).",
  "world": "dungeon",
  "object_type": 11,
  "monster": {
    "model_index": 7,
    "scale": 1.0
  },
  "monster_from": "ZzzCharacter.cpp:14099-14106, CreateMonster, case MONSTER_GHOST:\n\n    OpenMonsterModel(MONSTER_MODEL_GHOST);\n    c = CreateCharacter(Key, MODEL_GHOST_MONSTER, PositionX, PositionY);\n    wcscpy(c->ID, L\"고스트\");\n    c->Object.AlphaTarget = 0.4f;\n    c->MoveSpeed = 15;\n    c->Blood = true;\n\nNo Scale (1.0), no weapon.",
  "alpha": 0.4,
  "alpha_from": "AlphaTarget 0.4: the whole body is drawn at 40% -- the ghost is seen through. The game reads it off game/play_tuning.h's kSeeThroughFigure and kSeeThroughAlpha, not off this line: Play::fit gives the drawn body seeThrough 0.4, and the draw multiplies it into the body's fade (its own depth first, then blended; its shadow dithered by the same number), so a dying Ghost fades from 0.4 to nothing. This number is MU's record of it. The cook_one stage draws the bare mesh and shows it solid.",
  "move_speed_from": "c->MoveSpeed = 15, against CreateCharacter's default of 10: MU walks it half as fast again across the ground. The realm's move_delay (400, OpenMU's) paces the tiles; this is the client's glide between them, and not carried.",
  "not_ghost_note": "Three lines in MuMain test `Type != MODEL_GHOST` -- the blood burst at a death (ZzzEffectBlurSpark.cpp:456), a hit's reaction (ZzzCharacter.cpp:4859) and the footstep dust (:6412). MODEL_GHOST (_enum.h:864) is an *effect* model, not this monster's MODEL_GHOST_MONSTER, so none of them skips the Ghost: it bleeds (Blood = true agrees) and raises walking dust like anything else.",
  "profile": "monster",
  "rig_from": "Seven actions, slots 0 to 6, exported with --actions=0,1,2,3,4,5,6. Keys: 6, 6, 6, 7, 7, 7, 13. 35 bones. BoneHead = 20 (ZzzOpenData.cpp:3462). Play speeds are OpenMonsterModel's defaults; 7 has no override and is not in the multiplier list.",
  "sheets": {
    "eagle01": "ghost_eagle01.png",
    "eagle": "ghost_eagle.png"
  },
  "sheet_from": "Two sheets. Data/Monster/eagle01.OZJ, 64 by 64, no alpha, on the body (194 triangles); eagle.OZT, 32 by 64 with alpha cutting 9%, on the ragged hem and wings (66 triangles). Decoded under a ghost_ prefix: 'eagle' is MU's working name and says nothing of whose it is.",
  "cutout_from": "eagle is a .OZT whose alpha is the ragged lower edge of the feathered strip -- a torn hem cut out, as MU alpha-tests it.",
  "sheet_materials": {
    "eagle01": "cloth",
    "eagle": "feather"
  },
  "sheet_materials_from": "Read off the sheets at 6x. eagle01: a grey shroud in heavy draped folds, a hood's curve at the top and a pale fold at the right edge -- cloth. eagle: near-black layered plumes ending in a torn fringe -- feather, as the bird's.",
  "sounds_from": "ZzzOpenData.cpp:3455-3463: mGhost1, mGhost2, mGhostAttack1, mGhostAttack2, mGhostDie, then SetMonsterSound(..., 35, 36, 37, 38, 39) -- offsets from SOUND_MONSTER_BULL1 = 210, so 245-249, GHOST1 to GHOSTDIE (DSPlaySound.h:192-196), the five it loads, one to a slot. Wired as ghost_* in sounds.json.",
  "effects_from": "None. MODEL_GHOST_MONSTER is named in CreateMonster alone -- not in MoveCharacterVisual's or RenderCharacter's switches, not in the missile code.",
  "islands_from": "29 islands for 260 triangles, joined by position rather than by sheet: the big one (1, 125) is the shroud with eagle's feathered hem welded onto it, so the feather strip cannot take its own material. Every island is cloth -- matte, rough, the shroud's reading, which the dark feathers sit under without a visible difference. They arrived as skin, the monster profile's default.",
